# File: tests/unit/test_plugin_session_smoke.py
# Generated from: specs/193-fix-plugin-session-smoke-failing-when-the-herdr-window-is-too-short-to-show-every-mcp-server/requirements.md
Feature: plugin.session-smoke reads the whole /mcp list at any window height

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A connected server below the fold is found
    Given a Herdr tab 6 rows tall showing a 16-row /mcp list with a "↓ 10 more" marker
    And "plugin:nmg-game-dev:blender" is connected in row 13
    When the project.plugin-session-smoke provider runs with expectConnected ["blender"]
    Then it pages down through the list
    And it returns "passed" with "nmg-game-dev:blender connected" in its summary

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A missing or failed server still fails and is named
    Given a paged /mcp list in which "plugin:nmg-game-dev:blender" is absent or marked failed below the fold
    When the project.plugin-session-smoke provider runs with expectConnected ["blender"]
    Then it returns "failed"
    And its summary names "nmg-game-dev:blender" with status "missing" or "failed"

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: The /mcp artifact holds every inspected row
    Given a smoke run that paged through a 16-row /mcp list
    When its evidence is read
    Then the /mcp artifact contains all 16 server rows
